From d077a25d1b1c5059a66d934ec0931b4d63c303fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: a1go3 <116062404+a1go3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:18:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(proxies): tell a ClientHello nobody answered apart from
 a timeout

A frozen server port lets the TCP connection up and drops the ClientHello, which the delay test showed as a plain timeout. The core now answers -3 for a test whose error carries the HandshakeStalled marker the fork's core patch sets, and the proxies page, dashboard and tray show "No reply" for it. The marker is matched by method, so the core still builds against a stock mihomo.

Changelog: Delay tests show "No reply" when the server never answered the TLS hello
